  {
    "id": 17,
    "date": "2026-04-14",
    "version": "1.1.0",
    "title": "Virtual Training Portal",
    "changes": [
      "Virtual Training Portal",
      "You can now run live training sessions through Microsoft Teams, manage them in one place, and gate students through pre-final practice quizzes before the official assessment.",
      "- New 'Virtual' course type with its own admin hub at Admin > Virtual Training. Create virtual courses, schedule Teams sessions per student, attach a final assessment, upload a handbook, build pre-final quizzes, and add students all from one screen.",
      "- Students with virtual enrolments see a new 'Virtual' tab on their dashboard alongside the regular 'Courses' tab. Each virtual course card shows the next session date and a one-click Join Teams Class link.",
      "- Instructors control when the final assessment opens. The 'Unlock Assessment' button releases it for everyone in the course at once, or admins can override per student for special cases.",
      "- Virtual courses use purple styling to distinguish them at a glance from regular self-paced courses, both in admin views and on the student dashboard.",
      "- A 'New Virtual Course' button creates one in a single short form (title, description, optional cover image, choice of final assessment). Virtual courses do not need chapter content, only the final assessment.",
      "- Type-to-confirm modal protects against accidental deletion of a virtual course. The admin must type the course title exactly to enable the Delete button.",
      "- A small 'Add Student' panel under each course gives a live search by name, email, student ID, or national ID, so adding learners is quick even with a long student roster. Students already enrolled in that course are hidden from the search results.",
      "Pre-Final Quizzes",
      "Each virtual course can carry a series of practice quizzes that students complete before the final assessment unlocks. Quizzes are casual, formative, and intended to reinforce learning during or right after the live Teams session.",
      "- 'Pre-Final Quizzes' section on every virtual course in the admin hub. Add as many quizzes as you need, each with its own title, pass mark (default 80%), and a Required or Optional flag.",
      "- Required quizzes must be passed before the student's final assessment unlocks. The dashboard card tells the student exactly how many required quizzes are still pending. Optional quizzes are informational only.",
      "- Each quiz has its own questions, authored through the same Question Builder used for finals. All question types are supported (multiple choice, true/false, short answer, table fill, drag and drop).",
      "- Admin can lock or unlock each quiz individually. Locked quizzes are visible to students but they cannot start them yet, so instructors can hold a quiz back until they have covered the material live.",
      "- Quizzes are NOT proctored. No camera, no fullscreen requirement, no violation tracking. Students can move freely between questions and retake the quiz unlimited times until passed.",
      "- Student dashboard shows a per-quiz status under each virtual course card: green tick for passed, gold play icon for available to take, grey lock for locked.",
      "- After every quiz attempt the student sees a result page with their score, pass/fail badge, and a Remediation Report button so they can review what they got wrong. If they did not pass, a Retake Quiz button appears.",
      "- 'Reset Everything' and 'Reset Attempts' in Dev Tools now also clear pre-final quiz attempts, so testers can replay the full unlock flow from a fresh state.",
      "New Question Types and the Shared Question Builder",
      "Final assessments and pre-final quizzes both support a new family of question types beyond traditional multiple choice. Authoring is done through one shared admin tool.",
      "- Short Answer: students type a free-text answer. The instructor sets a list of accepted answers. Whitespace and capitalisation differences are ignored by default; the instructor can tick a box for strict matching.",
      "- Table Fill: students fill in a grid of cells. Each column can be plain text, a dropdown of options, or a Yes/No selector. Each cell is graded independently and partial credit is supported.",
      "- Drag and Drop: students drag image or text items onto target zones on a background image. Decoy items (which the student should leave alone) are supported and the question is graded all-or-nothing.",
      "- Question Builder is available at Admin > Final Assessments > Question Builder for any assessment, or directly from each quiz row on the Virtual Training hub.",
      "- Drag-and-drop authoring is interactive: upload a background image, click and drag on the preview to draw target zones, add items with optional images and labels, mark each item's correct zone or flag it as a decoy.",
      "- Item images and the background image are stored per-question in their own folders so deleting a question cleans up its files automatically.",
      "- The drag-and-drop player works on touch devices: tap an item, then tap a zone to place it. Desktop users can also drag and drop with the mouse.",
      "Handbooks for Virtual Courses",
      "Each virtual course can carry its own PDF handbook that students read alongside the live Teams session.",
      "- Upload one PDF per course from the Virtual Training hub. Replacing a handbook deactivates the previous version automatically. Removing a handbook deletes the file from disk.",
      "- Students see an 'Open handbook' link on their virtual course card. It opens a custom viewer in a new tab so they can keep their dashboard and the handbook visible at the same time.",
      "- The viewer renders each page in a way that hides the browser's built-in PDF Save and Print buttons. Right-click on a page and the standard Ctrl+S / Ctrl+P shortcuts are also blocked inside the viewer.",
      "- The viewer remembers the student's last page and zoom level per course, so opening the handbook again drops them back where they were.",
      "Better Remediation Reports",
