      "- Creating a new Final Assessment no longer needs you to invent a URL-safe 'Course Key' by hand. Just type a Title and we build a clean URL automatically. The Course Key field is now optional, with a live URL preview under the Title so you can see what the link will be before you click Create. If you do type a key, we still clean it up (lowercase, no spaces, no special characters) so the URL never breaks. If a key collides with an existing one, we automatically add a numeric suffix instead of refusing to save.",
      "- New Final Assessments now start with an empty Question Builder so admins can add their own questions straight away. Previously a brand-new assessment came pre-filled with 50 placeholder questions that had to be deleted one by one before the real ones could be added. The Question Builder also handles older assessments authored before this release without crashing when the option list uses a legacy shape.",
      "- Newly created Final Assessments are now immediately runnable without a server restart. Previously the system tried to register the assessment's take and result URLs at the moment of creation, but Flask refuses to add URLs once it has started serving traffic, so the new assessment's link silently never existed until the next deploy. Routes are now registered at a lower level that works at any time, so the 'Run / Preview Final' button works straight after Create.",
